#. i18n: tag Text
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 31
#: xml_doc.cpp:5023
msgid ""
"The AVEDEV() function calculates the average of the absolute deviations of a "
"data set from their mean."
msgstr ""
"A función AVEDEV() calcula a media das desviacións absolutas do conxunto de "
"dados con respeito da súa media."

#. i18n: tag Syntax
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 32
#: xml_doc.cpp:5026
msgid "AVEDEV(value;value;...)"
msgstr "AVEDEV(valor;valor;...)"

#. i18n: tag Example
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 33
#: xml_doc.cpp:5029
msgid "AVEDEV(11.4;17.3;21.3;25.9;40.1) returns 7.84"
msgstr "AVEDEV(11.4;17.3;21.3;25.9;40.1) devolve 7.84"

#. i18n: tag Example
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 34
#: xml_doc.cpp:5032
msgid "AVEDEV(A1:A5) ..."
msgstr "AVEDEV(A1:A5) ..."

#. i18n: tag Text
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 62
#: xml_doc.cpp:5050
msgid ""
"The AVERAGE() function calculates the average of all the values given as "
"parameters. You can calculate the average of a range AVERAGE(A1:B5) or a "
"list of values like AVERAGE(12;5;12.5)."
msgstr ""
"A función AVERAGE() calcula a media de todos os valores pasados como "
"parámetros. Pode calcular a media dun intervalo AVERAGE(A1:B5) ou dunha "
"lista de valores AVERAGE(12;5;12,5)."

#. i18n: tag Syntax
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 63
#: xml_doc.cpp:5053
msgid "AVERAGE(value;value;...)"
msgstr "AVERAGE(valor;valor;...)"

#. i18n: tag Example
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 64
#: xml_doc.cpp:5056
msgid "AVERAGE(12;5;7) equals 8"
msgstr "AVERAGE(12;5;7) é igual a 8"

#. i18n: tag Example
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 65
#: xml_doc.cpp:5059
msgid "AVERAGE(12.5;2) equals 7.25"
msgstr "AVERAGE(12,5;2) é igual a 7,25"

#. i18n: tag Comment
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 77
#. i18n: tag Comment
#. i18n: file functions/text.xml line 311
#. i18n: tag Comment
#. i18n: file functions/text.xml line 315
#. i18n: tag Comment
#. i18n: file functions/text.xml line 319
#. i18n: tag Comment
#. i18n: file functions/text.xml line 323
#. i18n: tag Comment
#. i18n: file functions/text.xml line 327
#: xml_doc.cpp:5065 xml_doc.cpp:6656 xml_doc.cpp:6659 xml_doc.cpp:6662
#: xml_doc.cpp:6665 xml_doc.cpp:6668
msgid "String values"
msgstr "Valores de texto"

#. i18n: tag Text
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 81
#: xml_doc.cpp:5068
msgid ""
"The AVERAGEA() calculates the average of the given arguments. Numbers, text "
"and logical values are included in the calculation too. If the cell contains "
"text or the argument evaluates to FALSE, it is counted as value zero (0). If "
"the argument evaluates to TRUE, it is counted as one (1). Note that empty "
"cells are not counted."
msgstr ""
"A función AVERAGEA() calcula a media dos argumentos dados. Os números, texto "
"e valores lóxicos serán incluidos no cálculo. Se a cela contivese texto ou "
"se o argumento é avaliado como falso, é interpretado como un valor igual a "
"cero (0). Se o argumento fose avaliado como verdadeiro, conta como un (1). "
"As celas vacías non son tidas en conta."

#. i18n: tag Syntax
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 82
#: xml_doc.cpp:5071
msgid "AVERAGEA(value;value;...)"
msgstr "AVERAGEA(valor;valor;...)"

#. i18n: tag Example
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 83
#: xml_doc.cpp:5074
msgid "AVERAGEA(11.4;17.3;\"sometext\";25.9;40.1) equals 18.94"
msgstr "AVERAGEA(11.4;17.3;\"untexto\";25.9;40.1) devolve 18.94"

#. i18n: tag Comment
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 95
#. i18n: tag Comment
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 396
#. i18n: tag Comment
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 1454
#: xml_doc.cpp:5080 xml_doc.cpp:5354 xml_doc.cpp:6251
msgid "Alpha parameter"
msgstr "Parámetro alfa"

#. i18n: tag Comment
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 99
#. i18n: tag Comment
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 400
#. i18n: tag Comment
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 1458
#: xml_doc.cpp:5083 xml_doc.cpp:5357 xml_doc.cpp:6254
msgid "Beta parameter"
msgstr "Parámetro beta"

#. i18n: tag Comment
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 103
#: xml_doc.cpp:5086
#, fuzzy
msgid "Start"
msgstr "Inicio"

#. i18n: tag Comment
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 107
#: xml_doc.cpp:5089
msgid "End"
msgstr "Fin"

#. i18n: tag Text
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 111
#: xml_doc.cpp:5092
msgid ""
"The BETADIST() function returns the cumulative beta probability density "
"function."
msgstr ""
"A función BETADIST() devolve a función de densidade de probabilidade "
"acumulada beta."

#. i18n: tag Text
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 112
#: xml_doc.cpp:5095
msgid ""
"The last two parameters are optional. They set the lower and upper bounds, "
"otherwise defaulting to 0.0 and 1.0 respectively."
msgstr ""
"Os dous últimos parámetros son opcionais. Definen os limites inferior e "
"superior, toamando os valores por omisión 0.0 e 1.0 respectivamente."

#. i18n: tag Syntax
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 113
#: xml_doc.cpp:5098
msgid "BETADIST(number;alpha;beta;start;end)"
msgstr "BETADIST(número;alfa;beta;início;fin)"

#. i18n: tag Example
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 114
#: xml_doc.cpp:5101
msgid "BETADIST(0.2859;0.2606;0.8105) equals 0.675444"
msgstr "BETADIST(0.2859;0.2606;0.8105) é igual a 0.675444"

#. i18n: tag Example
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 115
#: xml_doc.cpp:5104
msgid "BETADIST(0.2859;0.2606;0.8105;0.2;0.9) equals 0.537856"
msgstr "BETADIST(0.2859;0.2606;0.8105;0.2;0.9) é igual a 0.537856"

#. i18n: tag Comment
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 127
#: xml_doc.cpp:5110
msgid "Degrees of freedom"
msgstr "Graus de liberdade"

#. i18n: tag Text
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 131
#: xml_doc.cpp:5113
msgid ""
"The CHIDIST() function returns the probability value from the indicated Chi "
"square that a hypothesis is confirmed."
msgstr ""
"A función CHIDIST() devolve o valor da probabilidade do Chi cadrado indicado "
"para o cal se confirma unha hipótese."

#. i18n: tag Text
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 132
#: xml_doc.cpp:5116
msgid ""
"CHIDIST compares the Chi square value to be given for a random sample that "
"is calculated from the sum of (observed value-expected value)^2/expected "
"value for all values with the theoretical Chi square distribution and "
"determines from this the probability of error for the hypothesis to be "
"tested."
msgstr ""
"CHIDIST calcula o valor do Chi-cadrado a ser dado para unha mostra "
"aleatoria, calculado a partir da suma do (valor observado-valor esperado) ^2/"
"valor esperado para todos os valores coa distribuición Chi cadrado teórica, "
"e determina a partir desta a probabilidade de erro da hipótese a testar."

#. i18n: tag Syntax
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 133
#: xml_doc.cpp:5119
msgid "CHIDIST(number;degrees_freedom)"
msgstr "CHIDIST(número;graus_liberdade)"

#. i18n: tag Example
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 134
#: xml_doc.cpp:5122
msgid "CHIDIST(13.27;5) returns 0.021"
msgstr "CHIDIST(13.27;5) devolve 0.021"

#. i18n: tag Comment
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 142
#. i18n: tag Comment
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 161
#. i18n: tag Comment
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 848
#: xml_doc.cpp:5125 xml_doc.cpp:5143 xml_doc.cpp:5747
msgid "Total number of elements"
msgstr "Número total de elementos"

#. i18n: tag Comment
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 146
#. i18n: tag Comment
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 165
#: xml_doc.cpp:5128 xml_doc.cpp:5146
msgid "Number of elements to choose"
msgstr "Número de elementos a escoller"

#. i18n: tag Text
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 150
#: xml_doc.cpp:5131
msgid ""
"The COMBIN() function calculates the count of possible combinations. The "
"first parameter is the total count of elements. The second parameter is the "
"count of elements to choose. Both parameters should be positive and the "
"first parameter should not be less than the second. Otherwise the function "
"returns an error."
msgstr ""
"A función COMBíN() calcula o número de combinacións posíbeis. O primeiro "
"parámetro é o número total de elementos. O segundo parámetro é o número de "
"elementos a escoller. Estes dous parámetros deben ser positivos, no caso "
"contrario a función devolve un erro. O primeiro parámetro debe ser maior do "
"que o segundo, en caso contrario a función tamén devolve un erro."

#. i18n: tag Syntax
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 151
#. i18n: tag Syntax
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 170
#: xml_doc.cpp:5134 xml_doc.cpp:5152
msgid "COMBIN(total;chosen)"
msgstr "COMBIN(total;escollidos)"

#. i18n: tag Example
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 152
#. i18n: tag Example
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 171
#: xml_doc.cpp:5137 xml_doc.cpp:5155
msgid "COMBIN(12;5) returns 792"
msgstr "COMBIN(12;5) devolve 792"

#. i18n: tag Example
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 153
#. i18n: tag Example
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 172
#: xml_doc.cpp:5140 xml_doc.cpp:5158
msgid "COMBIN(5;5) returns 1"
msgstr "COMBIN(5;5) devolve 1"

#. i18n: tag Text
#. i18n: file functions/statistical.xml line 169
#: xml_doc.cpp:5149
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "The COMBIN() function calculates the count of possible combinations. The "
#| "first parameter is the total count of elements. The second parameter is "
#| "the count of elements to choose. Both parameters should be positive and "
#| "the first parameter should not be less than the second. Otherwise the "
